Write down the questions the battery does not ask yet

WIP. Adding `docs/WANTED.md`: candidate questions with no capability row, and the
decision each one blocks.

Why a doc and not rows in `content/capabilities/`: `tools/catalog.ts` requires every
capability to name a `probe` (automated/observed/solved) or state `established_by`
(derived). There is deliberately no slot for an unanswered, unprobed question — which is
correct, but it means a known gap currently has nowhere to live except somebody's memory.

The gaps, found while citing this battery from an add-on:
- no `block.*` id exists anywhere in 70 questions across 7 files
- nothing on light emission or its colour
- nothing on potions, status effects, projectiles or arrows
- nothing on item entities, despawn or stack merging
- physics has 5 rows, all falling/throwing/knockback — nothing on fluid movement

TODO before raising: check the framing doesn't read as a backlog nobody owns. The point
is citability, not a wishlist.
